  I could only see your file in a photo, and the right-hand side of lines
  5, 8, 15, 19 and 27-30 was cut off. Every line marked "RECONSTRUCTED"
  below is my best reading of a truncated line - diff it against your real
  file before committing, the truncated tails are almost certainly not
  character-for-character right.

  What actually changed, and why:

  1. Lines 13-17 of your version were hardcoded (JAVA_HEAP_SIZE 2048m,
     RUN_ARGS=""). No Jinja variable, so no amount of clean plumbing in the
     workflows could have changed the rendered output. They now read from
     the injected config, with your hardcoded values kept as fallback.

  2. Your "# >> CONFIGURATION <<" block sat at lines 24-30, AFTER the
     `exit "${EXIT_CODE}"` on line 22. That is unreachable - the script
     always exits before reaching it. Its intent is folded into the live
     path above the `su` call now.

  3. That block indexed `environment_jvm_properties[application.name]`, but
     `application.name` does not appear anywhere else in your role - the
     working lines all use `deploy_app_details.name`. I used
     `deploy_app_details.name`. If `application` is a real var defined
     somewhere I could not see, switch it back.

  4. Values arrive as JSON in env vars, decoded in group_vars - see
     group_vars_snippet.yml.

  Renders correctly under Ansible's Jinja defaults (trim_blocks=true,
  lstrip_blocks=false).
#}
{# Resolve injected config. `| default(..., true)` also catches the empty
   values you get when the deploy runs without the config workflow having
   set anything, so this template still renders standalone. #}
{% set cfg_env_vars = app_config_env_vars | default({}, true) %}
{% set cfg_jvm_args = app_config_jvm_args | default([], true) %}
{% set cfg_run_args = app_config_run_args | default([], true) %}
{# Your previous hardcoded heap settings, now only used when the config
   supplies no JVM args. This is the "覆盖掉 default 的值" behaviour: the
   role default stands until wbr-app-config overrides it. #}
{% set fallback_jvm_args = ['-Xms2048m', '-Xmx2048m'] %}
{% set effective_jvm_args = cfg_jvm_args if cfg_jvm_args else fallback_jvm_args %}
{# RECONSTRUCTED - line 5 tail was cut off in the photo #}
export JARFILE={{ app_folders.app_deployment }}/{{ deploy_app_details.nexus_gav_binary.artifact_id }}.jar
export SERVICE_ACCOUNT={{ service_account }}
export LOG_LOCATION={{ app_folders.logs }}/{{ deploy_app_details.name }}
{# RECONSTRUCTED - line 8 tail was cut off #}
export RC_LOG_PATH="${LOG_LOCATION}/{{ deploy_app_details.nexus_gav_binary.artifact_id }}.rc"
export CONFIG_DIRECTORY={{ app_folders.config }}/{{ deploy_app_details.name }}
export STARTUP_LOG_FILE_NAME="{{ deploy_app_details.name }}-Startup-$(hostname).log"

# ======== APPLICATION ENV VARS ========
{# From ENV_VARS in <env>-config.yml (图1: ENV: "dev", NAME: "foo").
   dictsort keeps the output order stable so Ansible does not report the
   template as "changed" just because a dict happened to iterate
   differently between runs. #}
{% if cfg_env_vars %}
{% for key, value in cfg_env_vars | dictsort %}
export {{ key }}="{{ value }}"
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
# (no ENV_VARS supplied by wbr-app-config for this environment)
{% endif %}

# ======== JAVA OPTIONS ========
export JAVA_HOME="${JAVA_HOME:-/usr/bin}"
export JAVA_CMD="${JAVA_HOME}/java"
{# JVM args are split into two parts on purpose:
     - per-environment sizing comes from config (JVM_ARGS)
     - structural flags stay in the template, because they depend on
       app_folders / the app name and are not something an env config
       should own.
   RECONSTRUCTED - the -XX: tail of your line 15 and the -D flags on your
   lines 28-29 were cut off; verify these against the real file. #}
export JAVA_OPTS="{{ effective_jvm_args | join(' ') }} -XX:+CrashOnOutOfMemoryError -Dlog.root.dir={{ app_folders.logs }}/{{ deploy_app_details.name }} -Dspring.config.additional-location=file:{{ app_folders.config }}/{{ deploy_app_details.name }}/"

{# From RUN_ARGS in <env>-config.yml (图1: RUN_ARGS: ["D"]).
   NOTE: your draft line 30 was building RUN_ARGS out of a `>>` log
   redirection. I did not carry that over - the redirection already happens
   in the `su` line below, and folding it into RUN_ARGS would emit it twice.
   If you did want the redirect to live in RUN_ARGS, move it here and take
   it out of the su line - not both. #}
export RUN_ARGS="{{ cfg_run_args | join(' ') }}"

# ======== LAUNCH ========
{# RECONSTRUCTED - line 19 tail was cut off; this is the shape your line
   implied: run as the service account, send startup output to the startup
   log, capture the exit code into RC_LOG_PATH. #}
su "${SERVICE_ACCOUNT}" -c "sh -c '${JAVA_CMD} ${JAVA_OPTS} -jar ${JARFILE} ${RUN_ARGS} > ${LOG_LOCATION}/${STARTUP_LOG_FILE_NAME} 2>&1; echo \$? > ${RC_LOG_PATH}'"

EXIT_CODE=$(cat "${RC_LOG_PATH}")
echo "Application Exit with code ${EXIT_CODE}"
exit "${EXIT_CODE}"
